# Valgrind suppressions for FLTK's display stack, outside pofltk.
#
# Under Wayland the display stack loads glycin (Fedora's libglycin-2, an
# image loader), whose worker threads (gly-rayon-N, Rust's rayon and
# crossbeam) sometimes show invalid reads and writes of 8 bytes in
# crossbeam_epoch, at addresses valgrind itself places in the faulting
# function's own frame on that thread's stack ("in frame #0, created by"
# the same function). That is valgrind losing the thread's stack bounds,
# not an overrun. TestGlut showed them in 3 of 13 runs on sway (5, 2 and 8
# errors; 2026-11-07), with no change to TestGlut or pofltk's GL part; this
# suppression took all 8 of the third.
#
# Only Addr8 errors whose top frame is crossbeam_epoch's (inlined frames
# count) are suppressed.
#
# The same threads showed it again in glycin's change_memory_format, by
# rayon (2026-11-13): 181 errors from 5 contexts in one valgrind-sway run
# of TestGlut, invalid writes and reads of 8 and 16 bytes, each address
# "on thread 37's stack, in frame #0, created by" rayon's
# bridge_producer_consumer::helper, the function at fault. Addr8 and
# Addr16 errors with change_memory_format in their stack are suppressed.
# Written from that run's log: 24 runs of TestGlut on sway under valgrind
# since showed no such error, so it hasn't yet been seen to fire.

{
   glycin-crossbeam-epoch-addr8
   Memcheck:Addr8
   fun:*crossbeam_epoch*
}

{
   glycin-memory-format-addr8
   Memcheck:Addr8
   ...
   fun:*glycin_utils*change_memory_format*
}

{
   glycin-memory-format-addr16
   Memcheck:Addr16
   ...
   fun:*glycin_utils*change_memory_format*
}
